      "title": "A proved turn start refusal can wait indefinitely for optional filesystem metadata",
      "evidence": "The default turn passes timeoutMs=null. A no-PID error defers completion to the filesystem observation and suppresses subsequent close. With no abort, no authored watchdog and a pending stat, no remaining branch can deliver the already-established failure. The base finished immediately on the child's error. A stalled lookup was represented in existing controlled QA with an explicit abort or finite runner timer. The no-watchdog case is derived from current source and was not executed in this audit.",
      "acceptance": "Bound diagnostic result waiting independently of a running model turn. With successful prerequisites and only the turn's no-PID spawn refused, keep a required metadata read pending, omit all run/node timeouts and never cancel. Within the defined diagnostic bound, return the existing fixed unknown-cause failure with definitely-not-submitted, no duplicate turn, no kill, no inferred timeout, no retained timer/listener. A later metadata result cannot replace it. Preserve timely factual classifications and stronger outcomes."
    }
  ],
